{
"fps": 30,
"tempo": 1.08,
"xf": 10,
"total": 4943,
"seconds": 164.77,
"end_card_f0": 4793,
"blocks": [
{
"id": "n01_chat",
"shot": "chat",
"t0": 2.6,
"t1": 19.155,
"f0": 78,
"f1": 575,
"text": "Monday morning, Manchester. Emma Clarke buys parts for Northbridge Cycles. She types one question: how many city e-bike battery packs do we have? Seconds later, she has her answer. So what happened in between?"
},
{
"id": "n02_harness",
"shot": "harness",
"t0": 19.705,
"t1": 37.334,
"f0": 591,
"f1": 1120,
"text": "Her words don't go to the model first. They go to the harness, the code around the model. Think of an assembly bench. Our rules. Her message. A description of every tool, all fifteen. Stacked together: one request, 2,139 tokens."
},
{
"id": "n03_model",
"shot": "model",
"t0": 37.884,
"t1": 51.43,
"f0": 1137,
"f1": 1543,
"text": "The model reads every one of those tokens. And here's the twist: it doesn't answer. It can't see the stock. So it picks one tool of fifteen, find_item, and writes its arguments as JSON."
},
{
"id": "n04_guard",
"shot": "guard",
"t0": 51.98,
"t1": 63.418,
"f0": 1559,
"f1": 1903,
"text": "Can we trust what it wrote? Not yet. The guard checks it against the tool's schema: the right fields, the right types. Then MCP, the standard plug, carries it to the toolbox."
},
{
"id": "n05_erp",
"shot": "erp",
"t0": 63.968,
"t1": 77.642,
"f0": 1919,
"f1": 2329,
"text": "Behind the toolbox sits Ledgerline ERP 7.2, a system from 1998. The tool calls it with Emma's own permissions. We never open this cabinet: data in, data out."
},
{
"id": "n06_loop",
"shot": "loop",
"t0": 78.192,
"t1": 92.769,
"f0": 2346,
"f1": 2783,
"text": "The result goes back into the context, and the loop goes round again. Search the manuals. Check the stock. Each lap, the request grows. Five model calls later: 6,600 packs, eleven days of cover."
},
{
"id": "n07_refuse",
"shot": "refuse",
"t0": 93.319,
"t1": 111.25,
"f0": 2800,
"f1": 3338,
"text": "Then Emma asks for more: order 2,000 battery packs from Voltway Cells. The model tries a direct order, and the tool says no. Direct orders stop at \u00a350,000. This one is \u00a3285,600. Raise a purchase request first."
},
{
"id": "n08_preview",
"shot": "preview",
"t0": 111.8,
"t1": 125.732,
"f0": 3354,
"f1": 3772,
"text": "So the model builds the request, as a preview. Nothing is saved. \u00a3273,600: above Emma's limit, so Daniel Okafor must approve. Shall I go ahead? Emma says yes."
},
{
"id": "n09_write",
"shot": "write",
"t0": 126.282,
"t1": 136.344,
"f0": 3788,
"f1": 4090,
"text": "Only now is anything written. Ledgerline saves the request, and PR/2026/04417 lands in Daniel's approval inbox."
},
{
"id": "n10_receipt",
"shot": "receipt",
"t0": 136.894,
"t1": 146.355,
"f0": 4107,
"f1": 4391,
"text": "One last step: the tool reads the record back. Waiting for approval. What Emma sees is what the ERP really holds."
},
{
"id": "n11_close",
"shot": "close",
"t0": 146.905,
"t1": 158.772,
"f0": 4407,
"f1": 4763,
"text": "One sentence in. A receipt out. The harness builds the context. The model picks a tool. The guard checks it. MCP carries it. And Ledgerline does the work."
}
],
